                        "entry_id": "143fd892-7a30-30fd-9370-0953b8f91b27",
                        "glosses": [
                            "one is unwell"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "predicative"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4be140ef-4536-4c28-82fa-9f452f0a8d05",
                                "sense_id": "8a7c97f7-ae64-313a-918f-75d2e9008088",
                                "text": "Ему́ ху́до.",
                                "translation": "He is unwell.",
                                "english": "He is unwell."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0ac283ba-668e-4376-b6ce-c9bc29c4d914",
                                "sense_id": "8a7c97f7-ae64-313a-918f-75d2e9008088",
                                "text": "1848, Давыдов, Дмитрий Павлович (Davydov, Dmitrij Pavlovič, “Dmitrij Davydov”), “Думы беглеца на Байкале (Thoughts of a Runaway in Baikal)”\nДолго я звонкие цепи носил;\nХудо мне было в норах Акатуя.\nСтарый товарищ бежать пособил;\nОжил я, волю почуя.\nDolgo ja zvonkije cepi nosil;\nXudo mne bylo v norax Akatuja.\nStaryj tovarišč bežatʹ posobil;\nOžil ja, volju počuja.\nLong had I been wearing ringing chains;\nUnwell had I been in Akatuy's holes.\nAn old comrade helped [me] escape;\nI came back to life, feeling free."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
